      },
      "text": "GENERAL SOLUTION: If (x₀, y₀) is one solution:\n  x = x₀ + (b/d)t\n  y = y₀ - (a/d)t\n  for any t ∈ Z, where d = gcd(a,b)."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-DIOPHANTINE-EQUATIONS.md#008",
      "path": [
        "05-DIOPHANTINE-EQUATIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:number-theory:05-diophantine-equations, git-history:number-theory:05-diophantine-equations]",
        "canonical_path": "number-theory/05-DIOPHANTINE-EQUATIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[diophantine, equations]",
        "current_path": "number-theory/05-DIOPHANTINE-EQUATIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:number-theory:diophantine-equations",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "number-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[diophantine, equations]",
        "section": "number-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Diophantine Equations",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FINDING x₀, y₀:\n  Extended Euclidean gives sa + tb = d.\n  Multiply by c/d: s(c/d)·a + t(c/d)·b = c.\n  So x₀ = sc/d, y₀ = tc/d."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-DIOPHANTINE-EQUATIONS.md#009",
      "path": [
        "05-DIOPHANTINE-EQUATIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:number-theory:05-diophantine-equations, git-history:number-theory:05-diophantine-equations]",
        "canonical_path": "number-theory/05-DIOPHANTINE-EQUATIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[diophantine, equations]",
        "current_path": "number-theory/05-DIOPHANTINE-EQUATIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:number-theory:diophantine-equations",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "number-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[diophantine, equations]",
        "section": "number-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Diophantine Equations",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Example: 6x + 10y = 14\n  d = gcd(6,10) = 2. Does 2|14? Yes (14/2=7). ✓\n  Extended Euclidean: 6(-1) + 10(1) = 4... wait, gcd(6,10):\n  10 = 1·6 + 4  →  gcd(6,4)\n   6 = 1·4 + 2  →  gcd(4,2)\n   4 = 2·2 + 0  →  gcd = 2\n  Back-substitute: 2 = 6 - 1·4 = 6 - 1·(10-1·6) = 2·6 - 1·10\n  So s=2, t=-1, d=2.\n  x₀ = 2·7 = 14, y₀ = -1·7 = -7.\n  Check: 6·14 + 10·(-7) = 84 - 70 = 14 ✓\n  General: x = 14 + 5t, y = -7 - 3t.\n```"
    },
