      "text": "FUNDAMENTAL THEOREM:\n  For any non-square D > 0, x² - Dy² = 1 has infinitely many positive solutions.\n  The smallest positive solution (x₁, y₁) is the FUNDAMENTAL SOLUTION.\n  All solutions are:\n    xₙ + yₙ√D = (x₁ + y₁√D)ⁿ  for n = 1, 2, 3, ..."
